pve-storage-drs (0.1.5) trixie; urgency=medium

  * plan/optimize/heuristic: a new capacity-spread objective term and gate
    (IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md section 5.3 (C7) and section 6) so a group with
    balanced I/O but data concentrated on a single storage still gets
    spread -- `objective.delta_capacity_spread` (default 0.5) and
    `gates.capacity_spread_threshold` (default 0.25, nullable) are new
    config knobs, linearized in both the CP-SAT and CBC MILP backends (the
    CBC path also fixes a real numerical-conditioning bug found via corpus
    replay: unscaled byte coefficients were badly conditioning the LP
    against CBC's simplex). The default payback horizon is raised from 7d
    to 365d: a migration's cost is paid once and early while its benefit
    accrues for the placement's whole lifetime, and the old week-long
    horizon rejected real but slow-accruing balancing benefit -- the knob
    stays configurable, with config validation now warning below 30d.
    `explain`/`plan`/`apply` reporting, the audit log and `plan --json`
    (new `after_capacity_spread` field) all carry the new term; the
    worked example, `fc-tier1`/`reserve-tradeoff` fixtures and the corpus
    Pareto-dominance check are updated to match.
  * topology+execute: a disk with an unapplied PVE pending config change
    (a queued edit or deletion) is now pinned so plan/optimize never
    propose a move for it (IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md section 3.8) --
    Proxmox does not reconcile a disk's `pending` entry when the disk
    moves to another storage, and `GET .../config` silently returns the
    pending value rather than the one in effect, so only `GET
    .../pending` can tell the two apart; confirmed live against a real VM
    on a dev cluster. `execute`'s preflight gained a sixth live re-check
    so a pending change queued between plan and apply also aborts that
    move. Wired through `collect-testdata`/anonymize/replay (a new
    anonymized `vm-pending/<vmid>.json` bundle file carrying only the
    boolean pending/delete signal) and the corpus scrub audit; bundles
    committed before this change replay as "nothing pending" rather than
    failing.
  * `collect-testdata --replay`: a shared storage's capture-node pick now
    reads from the same anonymized, pseudonym-sorted view that gets
    committed to `cluster-resources-storage.json`, instead of the live
    API's own status-tie ordering, which could disagree with it and make
    replay ask for a node/storage pair the collector never captured --
    broke `plan --replay` outright on a real 4-node cluster capture.
  * `collect-testdata --replay`: a range capture taken with `--step`
    overriding `config.metrics.step` (recorded only in a bundle's
    `manifest.json`, never in `config.yaml`) now replays correctly --
    `compute_disk_coverage()`/`_fetch_raw_quantity_series()`'s two-guess
    step fallback matched neither guess and failed outright on a real
    4-node cluster's `plan`/`show-load`; the mismatch handler now raises
    the real captured step instead of a third guess.
  * `collect-testdata`'s anonymization step now accepts a format
    extension on a volume name (e.g. `vm-101-disk-1.qcow2`, as PVE names
    a qcow2 volume on shared LVM) instead of dropping the disk as an
    "unrecognized name" -- confirmed on a real cluster, where it emptied
    `vm-config.json`/`storage-content.json` for an entire group while the
    live tool balanced it correctly. Live topology is unaffected; only
    the anonymization step regexes the volume name.
  * anonymize: a group's real name (e.g. `dc6_T2`) is no longer leaked
    into a captured bundle's `manifest.json` call-log free text -- found
    on a second dev-cluster capture, the same gap `_redact_free_text()`
    already closed for node/storage/vmid one identifier kind earlier.

