pve-storage-drs (0.1.4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * REVIEW.md seventeenth-pass fixes (findings Z-01..Z-08), tasked with
    verifying that generated `findings.json` files cannot contain
    confidential log lines -- the answer was "not quite": three more
    privacy gaps in the same free-text findings channel the 0.1.3 fix
    addressed one shape of. Both committed `tests/corpus/` bundles still
    carried the exact label leak that fix removed (it corrected only an
    uncommitted bundle) -- rebuilt from their own structured `sample_series`
    field and `SHA256SUMS` updated; the corpus scrub audit gained a
    structural check for the shape so this cannot recur silently. The
    per-disk coverage warning and the cross-metric-consistency warning both
    embedded a real vmid straight from Prometheus, including one outside
    every managed disk group -- both now rebuilt from an allowlisted view,
    dropping the finding entirely when nothing registered remains.
    `metrics.extra_selector`, when set, reached a bundle's Prometheus query
    files (and, in one shape not previously known, a `verify-metrics`
    finding message) verbatim instead of being rewritten to the documented
    anonymized node alternation -- fixed at the actual root cause (a
    resolver precedence bug), and the bundle now replays correctly again.
  * `collect-testdata --estimate` and the `support.max_series_points`
    capture-refusal check both now account for the 0.1.3 gigapipe
    workaround's actual, denser stored-point count (previously understated
    by 2x at the default config, more at a wider `metrics.step`/
    `metrics.rate_window` ratio) instead of the configured step's plain
    arithmetic.
  * Documentation: the 0.1.3 changelog entry and two code comments
    overstated the gigapipe workaround as having "no effect on an
    unaffected backend" -- true for every range-query path, not true for
    the `quantile_over_time` decision statistic, which is corrected here;
    the workaround itself gained the plan/manual/internals documentation
    it launched without. `tests/corpus/README.md` now names `local/` as
    where a bundle under review belongs and documents a repair procedure
    for an already-committed bundle, applied to this release's own
    `findings.json` fix. `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` no longer promises a
    bundle's `findings.json` carries `verify-storages`' report -- it never
    has, and never needs to: that report replays byte-for-byte from data
    the bundle already carries.

