pve-storage-drs (0.1.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * `collect-testdata`'s diagnostic bundle no longer leaks a live cluster's
    unconfigured Prometheus/Telegraf labels (a real guest hostname, seen via
    a `host` tag) into `findings.json`'s free-text "sample series labels"
    finding -- found by hand-reading a fresh corpus submission before
    treating it as clean. The message is now rebuilt from the same
    vmid/device/node-only view already used for the structured field next
    to it, instead of trying to redact an open-ended raw label dict as free
    text.
  * `verify-metrics`/`show-load`/`plan` no longer silently read zero
    coverage and zero load against a gigapipe deployment whose
    `/api/v1/query_range` (and the PromQL subquery form) returns no series
    at all whenever a query's own step is `>=` the range-vector duration of
    the `rate()`-family function inside it -- confirmed live on two
    independent gigapipe deployments, and exactly the boundary this
    project's own default config (`metrics.step` == `metrics.rate_window`)
    sits on. A new workaround (`metrics.safe_range_step_seconds()`/
    `decimate_to_configured_step()`) requests a smaller, whole-second step
    when needed and decimates the denser response back down, with no
    effect on an unaffected backend and no effect on replaying a bundle
    captured before this fix existed.

